{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205","id":5209104168,"node_id":"PR_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABNnyfKA","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205","diff_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/1205/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1205/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/statuses/21061aa532401398db70c59a596debf330f70744","number":1205,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add guarded campaign curation and canonical publication operators","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The ten-worker unmatched-ingredient campaign needs guarded source application and canonical publication for an explicitly reviewed multi-owner plan. These operators bind the frozen source cases, published proposals, independent acceptance, producer bytes and complete owner inventories before writing, then preserve recoverable receipts and native publication lineage.\n\nDepends on #1158 at `e000d66dd26ab053e9b17ce7bf8d3c873c3dde99`; the PR base is that dependency branch. This PR contains implementation, regression tests and review evidence. Campaign owner edits and release products belong to a separate dependent PR after scientific reconciliation. There are no maintained ingredient, canonical mapping, unified snapshot, workflow, threshold or pin changes here. No merge is authorized.\n\nCurrent code head: `16c39b63bc95d3e7978ddccc6280b0d57954f4a5`. Final acceptance is pending: independent review found the inherited Unicode application-path defect #1255, which is being corrected before campaign application. The complete final code review and full test suite are still running.\n\n- Source application uses guarded writers, genuine owner preimages, closed proposal/acceptance bindings, complete before/after inventories and exclusive receipts. Promotions preserve their actual unmapped origins.\n- Canonical publication binds actual native generation output and sidecars, policy history, projected alias checks and native receipts. Historical owner attribution stays historical; changing an owner does not confer scientific approval.\n- #1251 preserves inherited collision families consistently while refusing new collision pairs. #1252 permits bounded same-path rejected-record maintenance and genuine UNMAPPED-to-REJECTED retirement, retaining identity/name/path/history checks and refusing revival or new-owner evasion.\n- The explicit #741 demotion route requires an independently accepted exact relocation tuple, genuine published origins and no prior receipt chain on either owner path. MAPPED-to-AMBIGUOUS demotion must remove ontology grounding; the publisher requires no generated ontology or registry rows and removes every previous subject slot. It does not choose between Angustmycin A and C or provide role/export approval.\n\nAddresses #1174, #1194, #1195, #1197, #1198, #1200, #1214, #1251, #1252 and the bounded workflow prerequisite on #741. The earlier five adversarial findings and #1214 recovery-copy finding were fixed and independently re-reviewed. Their immutable archives are under `reports/unmatched_campaign_operators_1174_20261108/independent-review/` and `issue1214/`. Original failed probes and historical evidence bytes remain preserved. The [earlier final review receipt](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1205#issuecomment-6718353021) applies only to its stated earlier head.\n\nCurrent validation:\n\n- 337 focused cases passed: 197 source, 131 publication and nine real native integration cases. Those nine actually execute source application, pinned isolated Claw generation, publication and receipt verification using Claw `76c1ebeea3fc7f80bf1abe044688f298f390cfac` and the immutable eac469f1 history fixture. They verify all 27 historical receipt bytes and held-position continuity. They require explicit external roots and may skip in CI where those roots are unavailable; no workflow or gate was changed to supply them.\n- `just qc` passed on clean exact16c. Log SHA256 `b906a58ff032eb30fc58f5898da51f546a746209dfe8516a8e476670c8d16fe2`. All 3,672 captured maintained inputs, 14 executed Claw producer files and the historical fixture remained unchanged. Rule B4 reported its absent default ontology path and skipped; this is not an all-ontology label verification claim.\n- Full `just test` at exact16c is running with both external roots; the log already confirms the nine native integration cases ran. At the latest live check, 15 CI checks succeeded and pytest was still running. Final results will replace this checkpoint.\n- At ancestor9a1, all 252 then-existing source/publication cases passed and the same 933-operation corpus passed complete record-stage validation with unchanged selection/payloads and no new collision pairs. This is not full campaign prepare/application. W04's separate exact9a1 review confirmed the status fix but found #1255 during real Unicode-owner application. Earlier d691 approval is explicitly withdrawn by its superseding independent review.\n\nEvidence for current additions is preserved under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/`: `native-rejection-regression-fix-v1` (manifest `0a3416a54b35e579c2d5dd13468761a4145ae90820d1ab1fb3af0306603e209b`), `campaign-demotion-source-v1` (`18838c962d84264fd97427f6f1477b5cc7ef02b5647822297349721becf689ff`) and `campaign-demotion-publisher-v1/portable-v1` (`30b7e0a68a7ccead3794a103c7e3d5c8a428083ba43dc9e700d5a66bda5e8369`). Final reviewed evidence will be archived in the PR after correction and re-review.\n\nThe previous clean eac469f1 checkpoint passed full local QC/tests (5,523 passed, 116 skipped, 31 warnings, zero failures) and all 16 CI checks. Those results do not substitute for final-head validation. This PR grants no source-case, owner, role or supported-export approval. No maintained campaign application has occurred.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T06:01:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T12:02:23Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6f42aa79f5cd7bb36fb42804216e8525e3c4a408","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CultureBotAI:curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","ref":"curate/all-unmatched-source-integration-20261107","repo":{"id":1175495445,"node_id":"R_kgDORhCjFQ","name":"MediaIngredientMech","full_name":"CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","owner":{"login":"CultureBotAI","id":23321000